      {
        "name": "convert",
        "description": "Convert an HTML file to WordPress Gutenberg block markup.\n\nNative blocks: p, h1-h6, ul/ol, table, blockquote, img, figure (img or\ntable + figcaption), hr, pre/code, details, video, audio; loose text and\ninline tags become paragraphs. Wrappers (div, section, article, body,\n...) are unwrapped. Anything else is kept as a Custom HTML (wp:html)\nblock; script/style/head are dropped. Both cases are reported as\nwarnings (stderr; \"warnings\" under --json) — nothing is lost silently.\n\nPrints the markup to stdout, or writes it to --output (overwriting that\nfile). Needs no project. --json returns {\"blocks\": <markup>,\n\"output\": <path or null>, \"warnings\": [...]}.\n\nExample: html-to-gutenberg convert page.html -o page.blocks.html",
        "options": [
          {
            "name": "--output",
            "aliases": [
              "-o"
            ],
            "arguments": [
              {
                "name": "OUTPUT_PATH",
                "required": true,
                "arity": {
                  "maximum": 1
                }
              }
            ],
            "description": "Write the result to this file instead of stdout.",
            "metadata": [
              {
                "name": "x-rb-type",
                "value": "path"
              },
              {
                "name": "x-rb-default",
                "value": null
              }
